How can I use PHP to fetch data from a MySQL database and display it in an HTML table with sorting and pagination capabilities?
As input data, I have a MySQL database with a table called "employees" that contains columns for employee ID, name, department, salary, and hire date.
As a starting point, I can establish a connection to the database using the mysqli_connect() function in PHP. Then, I can use the mysqli_query() function to retrieve the data from the "employees" table and store it in an array. 
To display the data in an HTML table, I can use a foreach loop to iterate through the array and output each row as a table row. I can also add sorting functionality by adding links to each column header that trigger a new query with an ORDER BY clause. For pagination, I can use the LIMIT clause in the SQL query and add navigation links to move between pages. 
Here's some example PHP code:
<?php
// Establish connection to database
$host = "localhost";
$username = "myusername";
$password = "mypassword";
$database = "mydatabase";
$conn = mysqli_connect($host, $username, $password, $database);
// Retrieve data from database
$query = "SELECT * FROM employees";
$result = mysqli_query($conn, $query);
$data = mysqli_fetch_all($result, MYSQLI_ASSOC);
// Sort data by column
if (isset($_GET['sort'])) {
  $column = $_GET['sort'];
  $query .= " ORDER BY $column";
  $result = mysqli_query($conn, $query);
  $data = mysqli_fetch_all($result, MYSQLI_ASSOC);
}
// Paginate data
$page = isset($_GET['page']) ? (int) $_GET['page'] : 1;
$limit = 10;
$total_pages = ceil(count($data) / $limit);
$offset = ($page - 1) * $limit;
$query .= " LIMIT $limit OFFSET $offset";
$result = mysqli_query($conn, $query);
$data = mysqli_fetch_all($result, MYSQLI_ASSOC);
// Output data in HTML table
echo "<table>";
echo "<tr><th><a href='?sort=id'>ID</a></th><th><a href='?sort=name'>Name</a></th><th><a href='?sort=department'>Department</a></th><th><a href='?sort=salary'>Salary</a></th><th><a href='?sort=hire_date'>Hire Date</a></th></tr>";
foreach ($data as $row) {
  echo "<tr><td>{$row['id']}</td><td>{$row['name']}</td><td>{$row['department']}</td><td>{$row['salary']}</td><td>{$row['hire_date']}</td></tr>";
}
echo "</table>";
// Output pagination links
if ($total_pages > 1) {
  echo "<div>";
  for ($i = 1; $i <= $total_pages; $i++) {
    if ($i == $page) {
      echo "<span>$i</span>";
    } else {
      echo "<a href='?page=$i'>$i</a>";
    }
  }
  echo "</div>";
}
mysqli_close($conn);
?>

