Here is a Java code snippet that transforms the sentence "He is running" from simple present tense to present progressive tense:
```java
import java.util.Arrays;
import java.util.List;
public class PresentProgressive {
    private static final List<String> IRREGULAR_VERBS = Arrays.asList("be", "have", "do");
    private static final String AUXILIARY_VERB = "is";
    private static final String PROGRESSIVE_SUFFIX = "ing";
    public static String transform(String sentence) {
        String[] words = sentence.split(" ");
        String subject = words[0];
        String verb = words[2];
        if (IRREGULAR_VERBS.contains(verb)) {
            return sentence + " " + PROGRESSIVE_SUFFIX;
        } else if (verb.endsWith("e")) {
            return subject + " " + AUXILIARY_VERB + " " + verb.substring(0, verb.length() - 1) + PROGRESSIVE_SUFFIX;
        } else {
            return subject + " " + AUXILIARY_VERB + " " + verb + PROGRESSIVE_SUFFIX;
        }
    }
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String sentence = "He is running";
        String transformedSentence = transform(sentence);
        System.out.println(transformedSentence); // Output: "He is runninging"
    }
}
```
This code snippet first defines a list of irregular verbs, the auxiliary verb "is", and the progressive suffix "ing". It then defines a `transform` method that takes a sentence as input and returns the transformed sentence in present progressive tense.
The `transform` method first splits the sentence into words and extracts the subject and verb. It then checks if the verb is irregular and adds the progressive suffix if it is. If the verb ends with "e", it removes the "e" and adds the progressive suffix. Otherwise, it simply adds the auxiliary verb and progressive suffix.
The `main` method demonstrates how to use the `transform` method to transform the sentence "He is running" to "He is runninging".

